scratch/eliza/state/

# paperkit's own derived artefacts, written beside a project it grades.
# ⚑ THE PRODUCER ALREADY IGNORES THESE AND THIS REPO DID NOT, so `git add` over a
# paperkit project swept them in: `paperkit/layout.py` declares
# `DERIVED_NAMES = {".delta-cache.json"}` and paperkit's own `.gitignore` carries it.
# ⚑⚑ AND THE CACHE IS MACHINE-SPECIFIC BY CONSTRUCTION — it embeds an absolute
# `"root"` path and an engine content-hash, so committing it would make one
# checkout's layout a fact about the tree. The `.txt` is a point-in-time sweep
# whose every line reads `broken … repo is not green`, which becomes false the
# moment the tree goes green — a stale verdict that reads as current.
.delta-cache.json
.delta-report.txt

# Claude Code — project skills / settings / shadow-engineer cotype ARE tracked
# (versioned repo assets); only personal-local settings stay ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json


# local marker: mtime of the last green full build (pre-commit weekly gate)
.full-build-stamp

# uv-managed virtualenv (binary; deps tracked in requirements.txt)
.venv/
scratch/.venv/

# setuptools' staging copy of the two DECLARED packages (`packages = ["substrate", "scripts"]`,
# pyproject.toml) — regenerated from tracked sources by every build/editable install.
#
# ⚑⚑⚑ ITS ABSENCE HERE WAS A CENSUS DEFECT, NOT A COSMETIC ONE. Every module under
# `scripts/` and `substrate/` exists TWICE in the working tree, so a census that enumerates
# by path counts each one twice — and the copies are STALE, since a build stages whatever
# the sources said at build time. MEASURED: `selftest-contract` refused with 531 NEW keys,
# every one of them a `build/lib/` path, on a turn whose only change was `git add` over
# files that already existed.
#
# ⚑⚑ THE GUARD EXISTS IN ONE CENSUS AND NOT THE OTHERS. `gate_population.GATE_HOMES` declares
# its two homes rather than discovering them, and its docstring names this exact hazard —
# "walking the whole repo would sweep in `build/lib/` copies" — so the reader that anticipated
# the defect is the one census immune to it. A per-census exclusion would need writing N times
# and drifting N ways; ignoring the tree fixes it once, for every reader.
#
# ⚑ AND A DUPLICATE MAKES A RETIREMENT HALF-LAND. Deleting `scripts/check_private_ratchet.py`
# while `build/lib/scripts/check_private_ratchet.py` remains leaves the origin visible to every
# path-enumerating reader — the retirement reads as done and is not.
build/

# local hardware/DMI dump (do-not-commit machine probe data)
dmi.data

# jea/metalanguage Haskell shim build artifacts (source agdai_shim.hs is tracked; binary is not)
jea/metalanguage/agdai_shim
jea/metalanguage/*.hi
jea/metalanguage/*.o

# genlop-style per-dir build-time ledgers (machine-specific timing, parallel to the makefiles)
.agda-times.tsv
**/.agda-times.tsv
.decode-cost.tsv
scripts/.decode-cost.tsv
.build-times.json
.agda-profile.tsv
**/.agda-profile.tsv

# reuse catalog relational store (Ⓓ.catalog-db; derived from the .agdai cores, regenerated
# by scripts/gen_catalog.py — the markdown renders are committed, the .db binary is not)
catalog/catalog.db

# ⟡sched-batch: compiled helper (arch-specific; built from sched-batch.rs) + its build lock
scripts/sched-batch
scripts/sched-batch.lock
scripts/.gate-outcomes.tsv
scratch/.edit-snapshots/
.selftest-last.tsv
scratch/.cst-cache

# The summit drop zone: incoming letters must not dirty this tree.
# Ruling: ~/github/summit/proceedings/rulings/inbox-drop-zone.md
# Ignored from HERE rather than by a file inside it, so provisioning adds nothing to git status.
/scratch/inbox/

# ⟡estate: material scraped from a RETIRING peer repo, held pending an accept/decline decision.
# Same ruling and same reason as the drop zone above, and ignored from HERE for the same reason:
# provisioning must add nothing to git status.  This tree already carries ~4000 uncommitted files
# behind a red Agda gate, so a foreign repo landing in it would be indistinguishable from
# substrate's own unfinished work.
#
# ⚑ A SCRAPE IS NOT AN ACCEPTANCE, and this path is deliberately OUTSIDE the promotion gate.
# Adopting anything from here means MOVING it to a tracked path — a capability left here is one
# nothing gates.  (Live warning: scratch/tsdbprobe.py is staged-never-committed and summit already
# records a citation resting on it.)
/scratch/estate/

# bazel's convenience symlinks (bazel-bin, bazel-out, bazel-testlogs, bazel-substrate), created in the
# workspace root by every `bazel test` (substrate:W300). They point into the output base, so they are
# machine-specific, and bazel-substrate is a whole EXECROOT: a path-enumerating reader that descends
# into it sees a second copy of the tree. MEASURED: mtools' mikemol-repin read an execroot copy of
# pyproject.toml through bazel-substrate and reported its old 03749d5 pins as the repo's own.
/bazel-*

# Machine state and scratch that kept appearing as untracked noise in a ~400-entry status
# (measured 2026-10-10 with `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard --directory`): build and
# tool logs, the C compiler's default output, editor/merge leftovers, temp and spool dirs, the
# egg-info staging dir, and the agent harness's per-user state under .claude/.
.build.log
a.out
*.orig
_build/
_build.prev/
agda/_build.prev/
agda/.build-out.log
agda/.sourced-out.log
agda/.leaf-verify.tsv
.paperkit-tmp/
.spool/
.tmp/
*.egg-info/
.claude/projects/
.claude/plans/
.claude/*.flock
/catalog.db
